@startuml
title SRM Supplier Lifecycle - State Machine
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #334155
  ArrowColor #475569
}

[*] --> Draft : Start registration
Draft --> Submitted : Submit profile and documents
Draft --> [*] : Abandon registration

Submitted --> UnderReview : Validate submission
UnderReview --> CorrectionRequired : Send back with remarks
UnderReview --> OnHold : Hold with reason
UnderReview --> Rejected : Reject with reason
UnderReview --> Approved : All required reviews approved

CorrectionRequired --> Draft : Supplier edits permitted fields
OnHold --> UnderReview : Resume review
Rejected --> [*] : Close rejected application
Approved --> PendingSAPVendorMapping : Internal supplier number assigned

state "SAP Vendor Mapping" as PendingSAPVendorMapping
PendingSAPVendorMapping --> Active : Existing SAP Vendor Code mapped
and eligibility checks pass
PendingSAPVendorMapping --> Active : Mapping gate configured as optional
and activation authorized
Active --> Suspended : Suspend with reason
Suspended --> Active : Reinstate with authorization
Active --> Inactive : Deactivate with authorization
Inactive --> [*]

note right of PendingSAPVendorMapping
SAP remains system of record for Vendor Master.
SRM does not create the SAP Vendor Master.
Mapping requirement before RFQ eligibility
is a configurable policy decision.
end note
@enduml
